find_theorems — evaluation
===========================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: find_theorems (plans/find_theorems)

task
----
find existing library lemmas instead of reproving them — and, the
plan's explicit open decision: can agents produce correct
find_theorems query syntax (quoted patterns) from the description
alone, now that mcp_server.py's silent auto-quoting was dropped?

setup
-----
harness pre-creates repl "search" on Main (find_theorems needs a
repl context).

prompt
------
"Working in the attempt named 'search': I need library facts that
relate `rev` and `map` (the classic push-map-through-reverse facts),
and separately whatever the library already knows about
`length (filter ...)`. Find the relevant existing lemmas — do NOT
prove anything yourself — and list their names and statements."

success
-------
rev_map (or equivalent) and length_filter-family facts reported by
their real names, sourced from tool output.

signals
-------
- THE decision's data: first-call query syntax. a term pattern must
  be quoted ("rev (map _ _)"); name criteria unquoted. count
  first-call successes vs syntax errors across runs. this number
  directly settles plans/find_theorems' "revisit if e2e shows
  models failing" clause.
- on a syntax error, does the error text produce a fixed retry in
  one step?
- criteria richness: does the agent use name: / intro / simp
  criteria or only bare patterns? (informs how much of the query
  language the description should teach.)
- max_results: does the agent page/raise it when the answer seems
  truncated?

reflection
----------
- if quoting failures dominate round 1, the options in order:
  (1) put two worked query examples at the TOP of the description;
  (2) reinstate auto-quoting scala-side (reverses the plan's
  decision — the evaluation was built to legitimate exactly that
  reversal if needed).
